  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protecting children through strengthening schools, families and communities in Bangui, CAR.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(1) Quality of and access to primary/secondary education for children is improved in Bangui.
(2) Children feel safer and are better protected at school, in the home, and in the community.
(3) Vulnerable women have the skills to initiate profitable small businesses. 
(4) Two local partner CSOs have increased capacity.;(1) Quality of and access to primary/secondary education for children is improved in Bangui.
(2) Children feel safer and are better protected at school, in the home, and in the community.
(3) Vulnerable women have the skills to initiate profitable small businesses. 
(4) Two local partner CSOs have increased capacity.;</narrative>
  </description>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct Beneficiaries: 1900 (very vulnerable children  (6-16), women, teachers, CRC members).
Frontline Workers: 370 PTA members, local partner staff, CPC members). 
Others: 11080 students in 20 target schools, religious and community leaders. ;</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the enrolment and attendance of 1000 vulnerable children around 20 schools in Bangui as well as improve teaching and the environment.;</narrative>
  </description>
